[rtl8291eu]
{instruction guide} : https://askubuntu.com/questions/1156519/cant-install-rtl8192eu-linux-driver-on-ubuntu-18-10
$ sudo apt install git linux-headers-generic build-essential dkms
$ git clone https://github.com/Mange/rtl8192eu-linux-driver.git
$ cd rtl8192eu-linux-driver

	edit Makefile
		CONFIG_PLATFORM_I386_PC = n
		CONFIG_PLATFORM_ARM_AARCH64 = y

$ make
$ sudo make install
	<NOTE: Install with DKMS does not work

<Trouble shooting>
1. module 8192eu uses symbol kernel_read from namespace VFS_internal_I_am_really_a_filesystem_and_am_NOT_a_driver, but not import it.
Solution : add following declaration before the statement calling to kernel_read()
	MODULE_IMPORT_NS(VFS_internal_I_am_really_a_filesystem_and_am_NOT_a_driver);

[network setting]
 - USE nmtui

